From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:08:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 169/182] hjviewer: only SYSTEM and its owner can serve the
 Windows IPC pipes, and clients check who serves them

The main pipe (\\.\pipe\HJViewer\query) and the service pipe
(query_service) were made with GENERIC_READ|GENERIC_WRITE for Everyone,
which on a pipe includes FILE_CREATE_PIPE_INSTANCE, and a client took
whatever answered. Any process of any Windows account on the PC could so
add an instance of its own and be handed what the window, the tray and
the service send each other: the access password's ticket
(Data::HjvGuestPc), the options that carry the account's bind and unbind
requests and the "update now" signal, passwords being set, and it could
answer for the service with a configuration of its own.

A listener of these two pipes now gets an owner (the process's user) and
a protected DACL: everything for SYSTEM and the owner, and for Everyone
only what a client needs (read, write data, read the descriptor), not the
right to make an instance. A listener whose descriptor cannot be built
does not start. A client opens the pipe with exactly that access and,
before a byte of a message goes out, reads the pipe's owner and DACL: the
service pipe must be SYSTEM's; the main pipe may also be the same user's,
in the same session, of the same executable and not less elevated (the
window of an app that is not installed serves it itself); no ACE may give
anyone else more than the client access. The window of an app that is
not installed binds the pipe before it starts to host, and when the name
is taken it stays open without hosting where it used to end with -1.

Mixed versions (every call of an update, an install and an app that is
not installed, followed through both versions): an update or an install
ends every HJViewer.exe before the new service starts, so no step of it
crosses versions. What does not work, by the design of the fix: a 1.9.3
process takes no pipe of a 1.9.2 one (it was refused by 1.9.2 for its
path before), and an app of 1.9.2 or older that is not installed ends at
its start on a PC whose installed HJViewer is 1.9.3, because it asks the
pipe for the right this change takes away.

Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk 83e508cfdf7a7c1ab954ebb61073016ab6ce6ac5 (Fix/windows ipc server auth (#16755))
Against upstream's diff: the Cargo.toml hunk sits in our longer feature
list of the windows crate, and the Windows-only test of src/ipc/auth.rs
that upstream had already deleted (9997b7a) and that named
should_allow_everyone_create_on_windows is kept under the new name
is_windows_main_or_service_ipc. Nothing else differs; parity-tokio-ipc
d0ae39b, tokio 1.44.2 and windows 0.61.1 of our Cargo.lock are upstream's.

